{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following PyPy 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original PyPy 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nfrom sys import stdin\n\nn, k = map(int, stdin.readline().strip().split())\nmod = 10**9 + 7\n\n# Build adjacency list\nadj = [0] * (n + 1)\nfor i in range(n):\n    adj[i] = (i * k) % n\n\n# Iterative DFS using explicit stack\nvisited = [False] * (n + 1)\ncomponents = 0\n\nfor start in range(1, n):\n    if visited[start]:\n        continue\n    stack = [start]\n    while stack:\n        node = stack.pop()\n        if not visited[node]:\n            visited[node] = True\n            next_node = adj[node]\n            if not visited[next_node]:\n                stack.append(next_node)\n    components += 1\n\n# Compute result\nif k == 1:\n    print(pow(n, n, mod))\nelse:\n    print(pow(n, components, mod))\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <stack>\n#include <cmath>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nlong long modPow(long long base, long long exp, long long mod) {\n    long long result = 1;\n    base %= mod;\n    while (exp > 0) {\n        if (exp & 1) {\n            result = (result * base) % mod;\n        }\n        base = (base * base) % mod;\n        exp >>= 1;\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios_base::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    int n, k;\n    cin >> n >> k;\n    const long long mod = 1000000007LL;\n    \n    // Build adjacency list\n    vector<int> adj(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        adj[i] = (i * k) % n;\n    }\n    \n    // Iterative DFS using explicit stack\n    vector<bool> visited(n, false);\n    int components = 0;\n    \n    for (int start = 1; start < n; start++) {\n        if (visited[start]) {\n            continue;\n        }\n        stack<int> st;\n        st.push(start);\n        while (!st.empty()) {\n            int node = st.top();\n            st.pop();\n            if (!visited[node]) {\n                visited[node] = true;\n                int next_node = adj[node];\n                if (!visited[next_node]) {\n                    st.push(next_node);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        components++;\n    }\n    \n    // Compute result\n    if (k == 1) {\n        cout << modPow(n, n, mod) << endl;\n    } else {\n        cout << modPow(n, components, mod) << endl;\n    }\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.85\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-7.211902266135439e-05, -7.510157047363464e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -9.536697689327411e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -3.194758028257638e-05, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -4.0531076592742465e-06, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -0.011091128922998905, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -6.651657167822123e-05, 0.0, -0.04912157729268074, -0.0017028844449669123, -0.08894839882850647, -3.4570634852570947e-06, -5.757642793469131e-05, -0.08894512802362442, -0.05924252048134804, -1.966933996300213e-05, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -0.0020943391136825085, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.00965426117181778, -0.029706906527280807, -